WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/power-user/pages/DashboardsPage.tsx  (route /power/dashboards). The manual Grafana
  dashboard-JSON composer. It reads NO API hooks — it is local-state only:
    • PageTitle  powerDashboards.title  + intro paragraph  powerDashboards.intro.
    • <AINLDashboardComposer/> — the optional AI drafter, wrapped in withAiFeature: AI-OFF renders the
      manual baseline, AI-ON is propose-only (onApply → editor). This is a SEPARATE, AI-gated surface
      (see SCOPE below) — NOT part of this parity unit.
    • GlassPanel1 — the manual JSON editor: PanelTitle powerDashboards.editor.title, a <Textarea>
      (value=dashboardJson, placeholder=powerDashboards.editor.placeholder, aria-label=
      powerDashboards.editor.label, spellCheck=false, rows=12), and a Copy (powerDashboards.editor.copy)
      / Clear (powerDashboards.editor.clear) action row with a role=status line. handleCopy branches:
      empty-trim → copyEmpty; no navigator.clipboard → copyUnavailable; writeText ok → copySuccess;
      catch → copyFailed. The draft persists to localStorage "ai.dashboardComposer.draft".
    • GlassPanel2 — the curated panel catalog: PanelTitle powerDashboards.panels.title, intro
      powerDashboards.panels.intro, and a grid of the 6 install-wide CURATED_DASHBOARD_PANELS
      (name + description) sorted by name (localeCompare). The names mirror the Go
      AINLDashboardComposerPanelEntry catalog (internal/api/ai_nl_dashboard_composer_handler.go).
  Manifest unit page:power-user/Dashboards → requiredCount=16 = 2 panels + 0 charts + 0 maps +
  1 state (success) + 13 strings.

SCOPE  (no scope narrowing — the unit is exactly 16 items)
  • The page has NO API data sources (manifest "data sources: none — renders from navigation values /
    local state"). The ONLY declared data state is `success`; there is no network loading/empty/error
    branch to port. The editor's empty field renders the prompt; the curated catalog is always present.
  • AINLDashboardComposer is AI-gated and is NOT a manifest unit (a manifest scan for it returns nothing;
    none of its strings are in this unit's 13). The web renders the manual baseline — exactly this page —
    when AI is off. It is a separately-tracked surface; reproducing it here would be out-of-scope
    (prompt "Out of Scope: … components"). The model keeps the `applyDraft` seam so a future native AI
    drafter lands a draft in the manual editor exactly as on the web. No stub is shipped (ADR-011).

